WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:05.490
Mark your calendars, Keanu fans, because two
of Keanu Reeves' most anticipated new projects

00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:08.600
are currently slated to hit theaters on the
very same day.

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:15.160
John Wick: Chapter 4 and the fourth Matrix
film will both debut on May 21, 2021, creating

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:17.400
a possible conundrum for moviegoers.

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:21.240
It's certainly an interesting choice for Warner
Bros. to settle on that specific release date

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:25.630
for The Matrix 4 when Summit Entertainment
and Lionsgate already claimed it for John

00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:26.660
Wick: Chapter 4.

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:30.520
Unless audiences want to catch both on the
same day, they'll have to choose one flick

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:31.820
to see before the other.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:32.940
"Woah."

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:37.300
Whether the studios are trying to encourage
a double feature or see which property is

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:43.260
more popular, May 21, 2021 will certainly
be a big day at the movies for Keanu fans.

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:48.000
Since it was announced in August 2019, fervor
has been building for the fourth Matrix film,

00:00:48.010 --> 00:00:52.530
which marks the newest addition to the Wachowskis'
canon since the original trilogy concluded

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:55.140
in 2003 with Matrix: Revolutions.

00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:58.320
So far, The Matrix 4 already has a star-studded
cast.

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:03.220
Helmed by Lana Wachowski and fronted by Reeves
as Neo and his Matrix co-star Carrie-Anne

00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:08.560
Moss as Trinity, the cast will also include
Neil Patrick Harris, Jada Pinkett Smith, Mindhunter's

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:12.980
Jonathan Groff, and The Get Down standout
Yahya Abdul-Mateen II.

00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:18.280
As for John Wick, the franchise kicked off
in 2014 with former Matrix stuntman Chad Stahelski

00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:19.600
co-directing the film.

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:24.139
Thanks to mind-bending action and a standout
performance from Reeves as an expert assassin

00:01:24.139 --> 00:01:28.060
pulled out of retirement following the death
of his dog, the first John Wick film was an

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:29.119
immediate hit.

00:01:29.119 --> 00:01:34.029
It spawned two sequels John Wick: Chapter
2 and John Wick: Chapter 3 Parabellum . All

00:01:34.029 --> 00:01:38.929
three films succeeded at the box office, and
the franchise as a whole has completely changed

00:01:38.929 --> 00:01:39.780
the action genre.

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:42.340
Reeve's career renaissance has been a long
time coming.

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:47.090
After roles in varied projects like Bill and
Ted's Excellent Adventure and an adaptation

00:01:47.090 --> 00:01:51.930
of Bram Stroker's Dracula, Keanu dipped a
toe into full-fledged action films with Speed

00:01:51.930 --> 00:01:53.080
in 1994.

00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:57.640
Before long, the Wachowskis came calling with
The Matrix, and Reeves' career changed overnight

00:01:57.640 --> 00:01:59.040
thanks to his role as Neo.

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:03.719
Throughout the original trilogy, Reeves cemented
himself as a bonafide star, but he had a few

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:05.999
rocky years that followed his Matrix success.

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:11.240
In the midst of Matrix mania and shortly thereafter,
Reeves made a string of poorly received films

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:14.510
like Sweet November, 47 Ronin, and The Watcher.

00:02:14.510 --> 00:02:18.560
Though he appeared in critically acclaimed
projects like Richard Linklater's A Scanner

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:21.760
Darkly, nothing was quite as successful as
The Matrix franchise.

00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:26.379
During his down time, Reeves stepped behind
the camera, making his directorial debut with

00:02:26.379 --> 00:02:29.770
the underrated action flick, The Man of Tai
Chi, in 2013.

00:02:29.770 --> 00:02:33.910
Luckily, Reeves found himself reconnecting
to the world of The Matrix when he reunited

00:02:33.910 --> 00:02:37.120
with Chad Stahelski years later for the John
Wick series.

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:39.660
The franchise restored Reeves to his full
action glory.

00:02:39.940 --> 00:02:44.080
Reeves insisted on doing most of his own stunt
work for the first film, which received glowing

00:02:44.090 --> 00:02:46.000
reviews from critics and fans.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:53.489
"People keep asking me if I'm back and I haven't
really had an answer, but yeah, I'm thinking

00:02:53.489 --> 00:02:54.320
I'm back."

00:02:54.960 --> 00:02:59.040
Thanks in large part to John Wick, Reeves
is firmly back on Hollywood's A-list, and

00:02:59.050 --> 00:03:00.890
he remains as charming as ever.

00:03:00.890 --> 00:03:05.420
A truly beloved celebrity for decades, he's
even found time to laugh at himself in between

00:03:05.420 --> 00:03:07.180
his stone-faced role as John Wick.

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:12.659
In 2019, Reeves lampooned his own image in
Netflix's Always Be My Maybe, playing an over-the-top

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:15.220
version of himself in the charming romantic
comedy.

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:19.300
There's no denying that Reeves is once again
back at the top of his game, and is seemingly

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:21.060
better than he's ever been before.

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:25.620
It remains to be seen whether either Summit
and Lionsgate or Warner Bros. will stand down

00:03:25.629 --> 00:03:29.709
and change the release date for either John
Wick or The Matrix 4 of the upcoming films,

00:03:29.709 --> 00:03:34.530
but having both movies debut on May 21 of
that year might be a perfect opportunity to

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:36.290
celebrate all things Reeves.

